        <p class="slabel">Why we exist</p>
        <h2>An association built on the experience <span class="grad">of international students</span></h2>
        <p>Imizi Links grew out of the experience of its members, who came to France to study. Housing, a bank account, social security, a residence permit, a first job, we have been through each of these steps and we know what they really involve.</p>
        <p>We decided to share what we learned. Our goal is simple, to make sure that students arriving today have clear information and support from day one.</p>
        <div class="encart">
          <p><strong>The people who answer you have been through the same steps as you. That is what makes our advice reliable.</strong></p>
        </div>
        <p>The association is open to anyone settling in France to study or work, wherever they come from.</p>
        <div class="mission-points">
          <div class="mp"><div><h3 class="mp-t">Reliable, first-hand information</h3><p class="mp-d">Our guides are written by people who went through the process themselves, with real timelines, the documents you need and the right order of steps.</p></div></div>
          <div class="mp"><div><h3 class="mp-t">Local contacts you can reach</h3><p class="mp-d">Volunteers in Paris and the Île-de-France region, Lyon, Bordeaux, Marseille, Lille, Toulouse and Nantes, who reply to requests within 48 hours.</p></div></div>
          <div class="mp"><div><h3 class="mp-t">Support on the way to work</h3><p class="mp-d">CV reviews, interview preparation, and internships and jobs shared by our partner companies.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
